A||||27||Cliff Pennock||Some people...||||8||
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||09-12-2001||03:09 PM||||I visited a few other forums since I was wondering how people on other forums were reacting to the tragic events of yesterday.<P>I couldn't believe some of the sh!t I found. There were a lot of people (Americans for crying out loud) that were already sick and tired of hearing about the same thing and suggested to stop "whining" about it and move on (one quote: "Enough already! Let's talk about cars!" - this was on the LS1 forum). This was within 24 hours of the events.<P>Unbelievable. Are some people really this dense? Are some people really this heartless? I'm not even an American, but all I can think of right now is about what has happened... Thousands and thousands of innocent people have lost their lives in an act of unspeakable violence. This was in no way one of those "sh!t happens" kind of things. This was an attack against the free world and it concerns us all.<P>Some people just don't have their priorities straight.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Jaygee79||09-12-2001||03:11 PM||||unbelievable.  i guess some people just don't care||||reg||8
Z||000002||mrfiero||09-12-2001||03:13 PM||||Unfortunately there are always those who are only concerned with themselves (I can name a few on this list!).<P>Prioritizing your Firebird or whatever else came with an LS1 over the events of yesterday is just plain sick.  <P>I'm not going to go off on a big rant, but I find it disheartening to hear that some people are tired of being inconvenienced by the crisis in New York.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierochic88||09-12-2001||03:13 PM||||Damn.  Some people are so totally heartless it's sickening.<P>I'm not normally an emotional person, but on the way to class this morning tears came to my eyes as I was listening to some of the stuff on the radio.<P>Jennifer||||reg||1
Z||000004||Urchin||09-12-2001||03:15 PM||||Sad.  Self-absorbed people...  "if it doesn't effect me, it didn't happen" type attitude.  The unfortunate thing is that they don't see that it actually does involve them.  Or as you put it, involves "all of us".  IT's too bad.  Those types of attitudes are just as bad as those who were celebrating yesterdays events.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/final.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000005||beer_stud_21||09-12-2001||03:18 PM||||The stuff that happened yesterday was very very sad.  It was almost unbelieveable.  Like it was something out of a science fiction movie.  ID4 or something.  Now this is just the beginning.  Nato is going to get involved and I just heard comments on the news that the white house is considering this an act of war.  Which I am tending to agree with but which the idea really scares me.  I think we have already lost more american lives than we did in desert storm and this could only be the beginning.  I just hope it doesnt escelate into something huge!....  ;-(<P>-marlin||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierobaby||09-12-2001||03:26 PM||||wow some people are so heartless!! I normally am not a person to cry over things like this. but last ngiht and this morning I couldn't help but being moved by what people are saying. I gave blood I did my part to help and I hope everyone else does too ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||09-12-2001||03:32 PM||||Not to excuse them... I'm sure many really ARE selfish jerks... I believe some people have gone into emotional overload though and HAVE to have a break from it. Some of what you saw could be that.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||09-12-2001||03:42 PM||||I can understand people have the need to discuss other things, to get their mind of the events. But that's not what this was about. The things I read were from people who really couldn't care less about what had happened.<P>I don't even mind if you don't want to discuss the events, but telling other people that they should stop whining shows an incredible lack of common sense.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Hank is Here||09-12-2001||04:20 PM||||I must put a plug in here.  I will not let any act stop me from going on with my life, especially terrorism.  Stopping everything is  one of the side affects these lowlifes want to accomplish.  I feel by still working this is what we all need to do to hopefully put across a message that these acts will not stop the USA.   <P>By no means am I saying, get on with it, or, stop whining. I am saying just keep living.<BR>  <BR>As well, I am doing what I need to do now. I am not treating today as normal day; I am still getting done what needs to be done.  <P>In saying this hopefully NYC will take as little time as necessary to get back to normal operations.  I feel that it is a good sign that the Pentagon is not closed and did not close to whomever did this horrible act.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroMaster88||09-12-2001||04:38 PM||||Some people are just like that.  They dont give a damn about anything but themselvs, wont help anyone in need or give anything for a good cause.  Then they bit*h and moan when they need help and no one is willing.  I just cant believe some peoples ignorance sometimes!<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000011||dennis_6||09-12-2001||04:58 PM||||Q 102 (101.9 FM) A Cincinnati, Ohio station Had a caller call in about 7:30 PM tuesday <BR>9-11-01 and complain that the news was being too negative and that they need to stop showing footage of the WTC and just rebuild and pretty much seek a peaceful resolution and give up our anger because we are wrong to be angry.  Unfortunely the radio station agreed that the news needed to stop being negative and people should just be happy and rebuild.  I know everyone in Cincinnati  is not that stupid but that city is really starting to get on my nerves. ||||reg||8
Z||000012||dennis_6||09-12-2001||04:58 PM||||Q 102 (101.9 FM) A Cincinnati, Ohio station Had a caller call in about 7:30 PM tuesday <BR>9-11-01 and complain that the news was being too negative and that they need to stop showing footage of the WTC and just rebuild and pretty much seek a peaceful resolution and give up our anger because we are wrong to be angry.  Unfortunely the radio station agreed that the news needed to stop being negative and people should just be happy and rebuild.  I know everyone in Cincinnati  is not that stupid but that city is really starting to get on my nerves. <BR>Check out Q102's website all kinds of sympathy for the dead. <A HREF="http://www.wkrq.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.wkrq.com</A> <BR>I think Cincinnati's 94.1 is a much more moral station. <A HREF="http://www.wvmx.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.wvmx.com/</A> <P>Sorry about the double post.  Don't know how that happened.<BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/usa1017[1].gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/israel-clear.gif"">        <BR>It is indeed a poor man that only knows one way to spell a word.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by dennis_6 (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000013||Cheever3000||09-12-2001||06:18 PM||||I'm proud to be part of this Forum, and to be identified with its founder.<P>Those ignorant people must have a screw loose, but the rest of us who care are defending them whether they realize it or not.  They should have just a taste of what life is like in other countries for the majority of the world's population.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000014||tgowens||09-12-2001||06:31 PM||||Cliff, I agree!!! I was in Viet Nam twice - we lost a LOT of lives. The Gulf War cost us more.......but now, we have lost <I>thousands</I> right here on our own soil - we are at war but don't even know who with!!!<P>Yesterday, in the blink of an eye, fathers and mothers were not going home to their children, brothers and sisters would never attend school again, infants that never had a chance at knowing the world were gone. I am deeply saddened by all of these things but - there are insensitive people in this world, there are selfish people in this world, there are people in this world intent on harming defenseless unknowing innocent people just to further their cause..........now <I>that</I> is simply intolerable. <P>If the people who don't like the negativity would put their efforts and energy in stopping things negative instead of complaining that there <I>is</I> negativity, this <I>might</I> be a better world......<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Fformula88||09-12-2001||06:47 PM||||Thats just being disrespectful to those who have died, or lost loved ones.  It is simply rediculous to say those things, even if they are tired of it.<P>Beyond that, this has the potential of being a truly historic event with an incredibly positive outcome, all things considered!  There is some belief that thru Pakistan, they may be able to convince Afghanistan to turn over Bin-Laden without military involvement.  Such an accomplishment in the face of this "act of War"... to resolve it without turning it into a war and yet bringing those responsible to justice would almost be a revolution in foreign relations!<P>It would also send a strong message to terrorists that they are not outside of the reach of those countries who value freedom!  <P>Everyone has said this will change the world... it may just change it for the better.<P>My prayers and blessings to all who have suffered this week!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">   <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000016||AkursedX||09-12-2001||07:20 PM||||That's the society we have come to live in I guess.  It's pretty sad....<P>Yesterday, I saw Diane Sawyer on TV and she was saying about how after the buildings collapsed, there were still some people on Manhatten who were still doing their shopping like it was nothing. Now I know I'm considered pretty heartless, but that is just rediculous.  I think my shopping could wait at a time like that. <P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||TI_3VOM||09-12-2001||07:41 PM||||   I'm not sure where to go with this. Having lost my mother a few weeks ago, I can more than sypathise with everyone that knows someone in New York (or even knows someone who knows/knew someone). And being a veteran, the attack on the Pentagon was especially upsetting...the next ultimate "slap in the face". (the first being a hit on the White House or the Capitol) At first I was upset, then angry. Now I'm kinda numb. It's not from callousness. Guess I'm just a bit overloaded with all the sights and reports. I still watch, though. Gotta keep informed, involved.<BR>   The flip side to that is obsession. That's why I decided to go back to the forum a few days after my mom passed away. I needed to get out of the grief, before it overwhelmed me. That's why I'm here now. Just to see this post reassures me that we're all not single minded, pleasure driven, "don't bother me with reality" brain stems. Just because we're here doesn't mean we haven't felt the horror, the saddness, the anger. I did, and still do. Some of us just have different ways of coping. <BR>     <BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000018||johnt671||09-12-2001||09:51 PM||||That's sad.  Saw an even worse event on our local new last night.  A psychology dick from a local collage (won't name because I'm not sure I heard it right) said the attack was our fault because we are bullys and the terr. had no choice but to attack us.  Made me feel like the time we found an NVA headquarter in caves with better medical supplies than we had.  Along with this we found letter from Berkley Collage in CA telling the NVA they hoped they found the supplies useful in their war against the fascist Americans. Felt the same way when I saw and heard this pond scum.||||reg||1
Z||000019||2xsess||09-12-2001||09:55 PM||||Well, All I have to say is that people that can't think beyond their own life are shallow and not worth our time. If they had family directly involved you know that they'd want 24/7 coverage of the events. <P>The activity level of our camp here in Kosovo has dropped to nil, everyone is huddled around TVs watching for the latest developments. It's hard to tear ourselves from the TV to continue our mission. Our hearts go out to all those who have been directly affected whether it's a lost loved one or what ever. Unfortunetly we can't donate blood now or with in the next 3 months due to being deployed.<P>May all your prayers be with the victims of this awful tradgety. <P>Jeff<P>||||reg||1
Z||000020||MsBeth||09-12-2001||11:02 PM||||I almost feel bad for people like that ... <P>Hey Jeff you guys take care over there ok ... come home safe.  <P>MsBeth||||reg||1
