Z||000025||ChadMan||09-15-2001||09:48 AM||||I'm afraid we will here a lot more lefty talk from the entertainment industry and collegiate faculty in the next few weeks.  At a concert last night in L.A., Madonna asked the crowd to pray for peace and that President Bush "show some restraint" in our response.<P>Luckily, I think even the liberals in Congress aren't listening.<P>"The charred rubble and thousands of dead Americans lying just blocks from my office in Manhattan, and hundreds more a stone's throw from this very building, demonstrate we have no choice," said Rep. Jerrold Nadler, D-N.Y., whose district includes the toppled World Trade Center towers. "We must wage the war that has been thrust upon us." <P>||||reg||8
Z||000026||Raydar||09-15-2001||02:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChadMan:<BR><B>I'm afraid we will here a lot more lefty talk from the entertainment industry and collegiate faculty in the next few weeks.  At a concert last night in L.A., Madonna asked the crowd to pray for peace and that President Bush "show some restraint" in our response.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm soooo glad that the entertainment industry knows all the answers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000027||Taijiguy||09-15-2001||05:41 PM||||Personally, I've been glued to the TV all week. Day and night.  I even slept on the couch with the TV on, trying to sub-cousciously hear any news; initially about additional attacks, then about victims being rescued, and about arrests and new developments about who is responsible. I agree about feeling kind of sorry for the people who don't seem to have any feelings. I have to assume it's some tough-guy act, not to be moved by other people's heartache, or they are so afraid of their own feelings, they just have to shut down to what's around them, lest they have to acknowledge they have feelings. I gratefully confess that this has scarred me deeply. I say gratefully, because it reminds me that at least I have the capacity for feelings.||||reg||9
